{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-8266" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $z=2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}))$ in the form $z=x+\\text{i}y.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040761/state.json" "file_sha256" "76de1307fe67d56029e75aa810a918e50005e98c5ea50fe9d1777b2bcaa01af7"} {"question" "q-8266" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To express the number in Cartesian form, we expand the parentheses and substitute the values of the cosine and sine.\n\nSince $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{6}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{6}=\\frac{1}{2}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})) \\\\  & =2(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}+\\text{i}\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}+\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040761/state.json" "file_sha256" "76de1307fe67d56029e75aa810a918e50005e98c5ea50fe9d1777b2bcaa01af7"} {"question" "q-8266" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040761/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "76ddd8bc40b2572f7589606443b3219eca3e41dd79bc1b9ce4b8de8522cccc2a"} {"question" "q-8266" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040761/state.json" "file_sha256" "76de1307fe67d56029e75aa810a918e50005e98c5ea50fe9d1777b2bcaa01af7"} {"question" "q-8266" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "z=1+\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i}"] ["math" "z=\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\text{i}"] ["math" "z=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\text{i}"] ["math" "z=\\sqrt{3}+\\frac{1}{2}\\text{i}"] ["math" "z=\\sqrt{3}+\\text{i}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040761/state.json" "file_sha256" "76de1307fe67d56029e75aa810a918e50005e98c5ea50fe9d1777b2bcaa01af7"} {"question" "q-8266" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "z=\\sqrt{3}+\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040761/state.json" "file_sha256" "76de1307fe67d56029e75aa810a918e50005e98c5ea50fe9d1777b2bcaa01af7"} {"question" "q-107551" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $z=\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}))$ in the form $z=x+\\text{i}y.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040761/state.json" "file_sha256" "76de1307fe67d56029e75aa810a918e50005e98c5ea50fe9d1777b2bcaa01af7"} {"question" "q-107551" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To express the number in Cartesian form, we expand the parentheses and substitute the values of the cosine and sine.\n\nFirst, we find $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})$ and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}) & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute the values and expand the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}+\\text{i}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =-1+\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040761/state.json" "file_sha256" "76de1307fe67d56029e75aa810a918e50005e98c5ea50fe9d1777b2bcaa01af7"} {"question" "q-107551" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040761/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "76ddd8bc40b2572f7589606443b3219eca3e41dd79bc1b9ce4b8de8522cccc2a"} {"question" "q-107551" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040761/state.json" "file_sha256" "76de1307fe67d56029e75aa810a918e50005e98c5ea50fe9d1777b2bcaa01af7"} {"question" "q-107551" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "z=-1+\\text{i}"] ["math" "z=-1-\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{i}"] ["math" "z=-\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{i}"] ["math" "z=1+\\text{i}"] ["math" "z=1-\\text{i}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040761/state.json" "file_sha256" "76de1307fe67d56029e75aa810a918e50005e98c5ea50fe9d1777b2bcaa01af7"} {"question" "q-107551" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "z=-1+\\text{i}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040761/state.json" "file_sha256" "76de1307fe67d56029e75aa810a918e50005e98c5ea50fe9d1777b2bcaa01af7"} {"question" "q-321307" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $z=16(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{3})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{3}))$ in the form $z=x+y\\,\\text{i},$ where $x$ and $y$ are real numbers. Give the **exact** values of $x$ and $y.$\n\n$z=$\n{{field-1}}\n$-$\n{{field-2}}\n$i$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040761/state.json" "file_sha256" "76de1307fe67d56029e75aa810a918e50005e98c5ea50fe9d1777b2bcaa01af7"} {"question" "q-321307" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To express the number in Cartesian form, we expand the parentheses and substitute the values of the cosine and sine.\n\nFirst, we find $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{3})$ and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{3}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{3}) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{3}) & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute the values and expand the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =16(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{3})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{3})) \\\\  & =16(\\frac{1}{2}-\\text{i}\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{2}-\\text{i}\\,\\frac{16\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\  & =8-8\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040761/state.json" "file_sha256" "76de1307fe67d56029e75aa810a918e50005e98c5ea50fe9d1777b2bcaa01af7"} {"question" "q-321307" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040761/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "76ddd8bc40b2572f7589606443b3219eca3e41dd79bc1b9ce4b8de8522cccc2a"} {"question" "q-321307" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040761/state.json" "file_sha256" "76de1307fe67d56029e75aa810a918e50005e98c5ea50fe9d1777b2bcaa01af7"} {"question" "q-321307" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "8"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040761/state.json" "file_sha256" "76de1307fe67d56029e75aa810a918e50005e98c5ea50fe9d1777b2bcaa01af7"} {"question" "q-321307" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040761/state.json" "file_sha256" "76de1307fe67d56029e75aa810a918e50005e98c5ea50fe9d1777b2bcaa01af7"} {"question" "q-321307" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "8\\sqrt{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040761/state.json" "file_sha256" "76de1307fe67d56029e75aa810a918e50005e98c5ea50fe9d1777b2bcaa01af7"} {"question" "q-321424" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $z=\\frac{6}{1+\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i}}$ in the form $r(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ).$ Give the **exact** values of $r$ and $\\theta ,$ in **radians** from $[0,2\\pi ).$\n\n$z=$\n{{field-1}}$\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡(${{field-2}}$)+i\\operatorname{sin}⁡(${{field-3}}$))$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040761/state.json" "file_sha256" "76de1307fe67d56029e75aa810a918e50005e98c5ea50fe9d1777b2bcaa01af7"} {"question" "q-321424" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we express the given complex number in the form $z=x+y\\text{i}.$ To do this, we remove $\\text{i}$ from the denominator by multiplying the numerator and denominator of $z$ by the complex conjugate of the denominator, which is $1-\\sqrt{3}\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =\\frac{6}{1+\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6(1-\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i})}{(1+\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i})(1-\\sqrt{3}\\text{i})} \\\\  & =\\frac{6(1-\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i})}{{1}^{2}-(\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6(1-\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i})}{1-(-3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{6(1-\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i})}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn polar form, $r$ represents the magnitude $|z|.$ For a complex number $z=x+y\\text{i},$ the magnitude of $z$ is given by\n\n$$\n|z|=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nSo, for $z=\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\text{i},$ the magnitude is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}+{(\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}+\\frac{27}{4}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn polar form, $\\theta $  represents the argument $\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z).$ Since $x=\\frac{3}{2}>0$ and $y=-\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2}<0,$ $z$ lies in the fourth quadrant. So, we can find $\\theta $ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =2\\pi -\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{|y|}{x}) \\\\  & =2\\pi -\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2}}{\\frac{3}{2}}) \\\\  & =2\\pi -\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the complex number $z$ in polar form:\n\n$$\nz=3(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{3})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{3}))\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040761/state.json" "file_sha256" "76de1307fe67d56029e75aa810a918e50005e98c5ea50fe9d1777b2bcaa01af7"} {"question" "q-321424" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040761/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "76ddd8bc40b2572f7589606443b3219eca3e41dd79bc1b9ce4b8de8522cccc2a"} {"question" "q-321424" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040761/state.json" "file_sha256" "76de1307fe67d56029e75aa810a918e50005e98c5ea50fe9d1777b2bcaa01af7"} {"question" "q-321424" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040761/state.json" "file_sha256" "76de1307fe67d56029e75aa810a918e50005e98c5ea50fe9d1777b2bcaa01af7"} {"question" "q-321424" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040761/state.json" "file_sha256" "76de1307fe67d56029e75aa810a918e50005e98c5ea50fe9d1777b2bcaa01af7"} {"question" "q-321424" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5\\pi}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040761/state.json" "file_sha256" "76de1307fe67d56029e75aa810a918e50005e98c5ea50fe9d1777b2bcaa01af7"} {"question" "q-321424" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040761/state.json" "file_sha256" "76de1307fe67d56029e75aa810a918e50005e98c5ea50fe9d1777b2bcaa01af7"} {"question" "q-321424" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5\\pi}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040761/state.json" "file_sha256" "76de1307fe67d56029e75aa810a918e50005e98c5ea50fe9d1777b2bcaa01af7"} {"question" "q-324223" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $z=\\frac{3-5\\text{i}}{4+2\\,\\text{i}}$ in the form $r(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ).$ Give the **exact** value of $r$ and round $\\theta $ in **radians** from $[0,2\\pi )$ to **two decimal places**.\n\n$z=$\n{{field-1}}$\\cdot (cos$ \n$(${{field-2}}$)$\n$+\\,isin$\n$(${{field-3}}$))$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040761/state.json" "file_sha256" "76de1307fe67d56029e75aa810a918e50005e98c5ea50fe9d1777b2bcaa01af7"} {"question" "q-324223" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we express the given complex number in the form $z=x+y\\text{i}.$ To do this, we remove $\\text{i}$ from the denominator by multiplying the numerator and denominator of $z$ by the complex conjugate of the denominator, which is $4-2\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =\\frac{3-5\\text{i}}{4+2\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(3-5\\text{i})(4-2\\text{i})}{(4+2\\text{i})(4-2\\text{i})} \\\\  & =\\frac{12-6\\text{i}-20\\text{i}+10{\\text{i}}^{2}}{{4}^{2}-(2\\text{i})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12-26\\text{i}-10}{16-(-4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2-26\\text{i}}{20} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}-\\frac{13}{10}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn polar form, $r$ represents the magnitude $|z|.$ For a complex number $z=x+y\\text{i},$ the magnitude of $z$ is given by\n\n$$\n|z|=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nSo, for $z=\\frac{1}{10}-\\frac{13}{10}\\text{i},$ the magnitude is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{1}{10})}^{2}+{(-\\frac{13}{10})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1+169}{100}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{170}{100}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{170}}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{170}}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn polar form, $\\theta $  represents the argument $\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z).$ Since $x=\\frac{1}{10}$ and $y=-\\frac{13}{10},$ $z$ lies in the fourth quadrant. So, we can find $\\theta $ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =2\\pi -\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{|y|}{x}) \\\\  & =2\\pi -\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\frac{13}{10}}{\\frac{1}{10}}) \\\\  & =2\\pi -\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(13) \\\\  & ≈2\\pi -1.49 \\\\  & ≈4.79,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places. \n\nFinally, we write the complex number $z$ in polar form:\n\n$$\nz=\\frac{\\sqrt{170}}{10}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4.79)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4.79))\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040761/state.json" "file_sha256" "76de1307fe67d56029e75aa810a918e50005e98c5ea50fe9d1777b2bcaa01af7"} {"question" "q-324223" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040761/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "76ddd8bc40b2572f7589606443b3219eca3e41dd79bc1b9ce4b8de8522cccc2a"} {"question" "q-324223" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040761/state.json" "file_sha256" "76de1307fe67d56029e75aa810a918e50005e98c5ea50fe9d1777b2bcaa01af7"} {"question" "q-324223" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{170}}{10}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040761/state.json" "file_sha256" "76de1307fe67d56029e75aa810a918e50005e98c5ea50fe9d1777b2bcaa01af7"} {"question" "q-324223" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040761/state.json" "file_sha256" "76de1307fe67d56029e75aa810a918e50005e9